{"id":"h229","run":2,"role":"test_wrong","category":"science-physics","question":"A house near a lake is kept warm by a heat engine. In winter, water from beneath the ice covering the lake is pumped through the heat engine. Heat is extracted until the water is on the point of freezing when it is ejected. The outside air is used as a sink. Assume that the air temperature is -15 °C and the temperature of the water from the lake is 2°C. Calculate the rate at which water must be pumped to the engine. The efficiency of the engine is one-fifth that of a Carnot engine and the house requires 10 kW.\nIs the correct answer \"102.4 liters/s\"?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"no","correct":false,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"The answer 102.4 L/s is not correct; the rate is about 97 L/s.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The reservoir temperatures are T_H = 275 K (lake water) and T_C = 258 K (air).","confidence":0.95,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The Carnot efficiency is about 0.0618, so the actual efficiency is about 0.01236.","confidence":0.95,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Each kg of water cooled from 2 °C to 0 °C yields about 8.37 kJ of heat.","confidence":0.95,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"If the 10 kW is the engine's work output, the heat input needed is about 809 kW.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The resulting flow rate is about 96.6 kg/s, or about 97 L/s.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"A flow of 102.4 L/s would require about 857 kW of heat input, which does not follow from the given data.","confidence":0.8,"lean":-1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"If the 10 kW is heat delivered to the house, the flow would be about 1.2 kg/s, which does not give 102.4 L/s either.","confidence":0.75,"lean":-1,"theta":1.1781,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Latent heat should not be included because the water is only cooled and not frozen; including it would give about 2.4 kg/s.","confidence":0.8,"lean":-1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":4,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":5,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":4,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":5,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":6,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":7,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":8,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":4,"j":5,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":4,"j":7,"J":-0.6,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":5,"j":7,"J":-0.6,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":5,"j":8,"J":-0.5,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":6,"j":7,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":6,"j":8,"J":0.2,"relation":"supports"}],"readout_weights":[0.1667,0.0,0.0,0.0,0.1667,0.1667,0.1667,0.1667,0.1667],"stages":[{"stage":"encode","qubits":[{"amp":0.9877,"phase":-3.1416,"p_yes":0.0062,"bloch":[-0.9877,-0.0,0.1564],"purity":1.0},{"amp":0.9969,"phase":-3.1416,"p_yes":0.0015,"bloch":[-0.9969,-0.0,0.0785],"purity":1.0},{"amp":0.9969,"phase":-3.1416,"p_yes":0.0015,"bloch":[-0.9969,-0.0,0.0785],"purity":1.0},{"amp":0.9969,"phase":-3.1416,"p_yes":0.0015,"bloch":[-0.9969,-0.0,0.0785],"purity":1.0},{"amp":0.9877,"phase":-3.1416,"p_yes":0.0062,"bloch":[-0.9877,-0.0,0.1564],"purity":1.0},{"amp":0.9877,"phase":-3.1416,"p_yes":0.0062,"bloch":[-0.9877,-0.0,0.1564],"purity":1.0},{"amp":0.9511,"phase":3.1416,"p_yes":0.0245,"bloch":[-0.9511,0.0,0.309],"purity":1.0},{"amp":0.9239,"phase":3.1416,"p_yes":0.0381,"bloch":[-0.9239,0.0,0.3827],"purity":1.0},{"amp":0.9511,"phase":3.1416,"p_yes":0.0245,"bloch":[-0.9511,0.0,0.309],"purity":1.0}],"p_yes":0.0,"p_strong_yes":0.0,"p_strong_no":0.9999,